{"name":"Baby Jane","hex":"#d0a7a8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.\n\nA very young human, even if not yet born.","A very young human, even if not yet born."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"jane","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A silver Genovese coin, first used in England in the 14th century."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Jane, a woman.","Alternative spelling of jean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jane"}],"entries":[{"title":"What Ever Happened to Baby Jane? (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"What Ever Happened to Baby Jane? is an American psychological horror novel by Henry Farrell published in 1960 by Rinehart & Company. The novel has earned a cult following, and has been adapted for the screen twice, in 1962 and 1991."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/aa/WhatEverHappenedToBabyJane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_Ever_Happened_to_Baby_Jane%3F_(novel)"},{"title":"Sofi Oksanen","blocks":[{"text":"Sofi-Elina Oksanen is a Finnish writer and playwright. Oksanen has published six novels, of which \"Purge\" has gained the widest recognition. She has received several international and domestic awards for her literary work. Her work has been translated into more than 40 languages and sold more than two million copies. Oksanen has been called \"Finnish-Estonian Charles Dickens\" and her work has often been compared to Margaret Atwood's novels. Oksanen is actively involved in public debate in Finland and comments on current issues in her columns and various talk shows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sofi_Oksanen_-_Buchmesse_Wien_2022_%28b%29.JPG/330px-Sofi_Oksanen_-_Buchmesse_Wien_2022_%28b%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sofi_Oksanen"},{"title":"Baby Jane (Rod Stewart song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Baby Jane\" is a 1983 song by British singer Rod Stewart, written by Stewart and Jay Davis. It was released as the lead single from his twelfth studio album, Body Wishes. Produced by Stewart, Tom Dowd, George Cutko and Jim Cregan, it was his most successful single since \"Da Ya Think I'm Sexy?\" in 1978, peaking at No. 1 in the UK remaining at the top of the chart for three weeks. In the United States, the song was also a hit, peaking at No. 14 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/99/BabyJane.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Jane_(Rod_Stewart_song)"},{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Sofia_Oksanen%2C_vinnare_av_Nordiska_radets_litteraturpris_2010.jpg/500px-Sofia_Oksanen%2C_vinnare_av_Nordiska_radets_litteraturpris_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum